   "logo_local": "/static/images/brands/pickalbatros_logo.png",
   "description": "Pickalbatros is an Egyptian hospitality group operating a portfolio of upscale and upper upscale all-inclusive resorts across North Africa and the Middle East, with a growing presence in Morocco. In Casablanca it has bought two city hotels that keep their Accor brands: the Sofitel Casablanca Tour Blanche, from Risma (final contract April 2026), and the Mövenpick Hotel Casablanca. The group's Moroccan resorts are concentrated in Marrakech and Agadir, where it operates six large-scale resort properties ranging from family-oriented all-inclusive clubs to adults-only beachfront resorts and golf properties. Pickalbatros targets the European and regional leisure travel market with a consistent all-inclusive product offering that combines extensive amenities, entertainment programming, and prime resort locations. The group's expansion into Morocco reflects its confidence in the country's growing appeal as a year-round leisure destination for European and Middle Eastern travelers.",
